  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef cv_sobel_edges(image: list) -> dict:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Sobel Edge Detection** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef cv_sobel_edges(image: list) -> dict:\n    img = np.array(image, dtype=np.float64)\n    H, W = img.shape\n    pad = np.pad(img, ((1, 1), (1, 1)), mode='constant')\n    kx = np.array([[-1, 0, 1], [-2, 0, 2], [-1, 0, 1]], dtype=np.float64)\n    ky = np.array([[-1, -2, -1], [0, 0, 0], [1, 2, 1]], dtype=np.float64)\n    gx, gy = np.zeros((H, W)), np.zeros((H, W))\n    for i in range(H):\n        for j in range(W):\n            p = pad[i:i+3, j:j+3]\n            gx[i, j] = np.sum(p * kx)\n            gy[i, j] = np.sum(p * ky)\n    return {'grad_x': np.round(gx, 4).tolist(), 'grad_y': np.round(gy, 4).tolist(), 'magnitude': np.round(np.sqrt(gx**2 + gy**2), 4).tolist()}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
